  "summary": "The unification of Italy was proclaimed on 17 March 1861 at Palazzo Carignano in Turin, where the Chamber of Deputies sat. The new Kingdom of Italy joined most of the peninsula under the House of Savoy, with Victor Emmanuel II as its first king. Italy went on to incorporate Venetia and the former Papal States, including Rome, by 1871.",
